Subject: Do not destroy a dropped map entry again when unserialization fails
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

MSGPACK_UNSERIALIZE_FINISH_MAP_ITEM() destroys a key and value that are not
inserted anywhere (the metadata entries of php_only maps, values for keys
that cannot be used), but an array or object value stays in var_hash. When
the input then turns out to be invalid, msgpack_unserialize_var_destroy()
destroys every var_hash entry and freed that value a second time: a use
after free reachable from msgpack_unserialize() on untrusted data, for
example "\x82\xc0\x91\x01\xc0". This is what tests/034.phpt, marked XFAIL
upstream, hit as "zend_mm_heap corrupted". Clear such entries.

--- a/msgpack_unpack.c
+++ b/msgpack_unpack.c
@@ -55,7 +55,15 @@
 #define MSGPACK_UNSERIALIZE_FINISH_MAP_ITEM(_unpack, _key, _val) \
     zval_ptr_dtor(_key);                                         \
     zval_ptr_dtor(_val);                                         \
-    MSGPACK_UNSERIALIZE_FINISH_ITEM(_unpack, _key, _val);
+    MSGPACK_UNSERIALIZE_FINISH_ITEM(_unpack, _key, _val);        \
+    /* Arrays and objects stay in var_hash, which destroys its  \
+     * entries again when unserialization fails. */             \
+    if (!MSGPACK_IS_STACK_VALUE(_key)) {                         \
+        ZVAL_UNDEF(_key);                                        \
+    }                                                            \
+    if (!MSGPACK_IS_STACK_VALUE(_val)) {                         \
+        ZVAL_UNDEF(_val);                                        \
+    }
 
 #define UNSET_MAGIC_METHODS(_ce)                                 \
     __get = _ce->__get;                                          \
